# Phase 21: Refinements & New Features

## Answers to Your Questions (Before We Proceed)

1. **How Property Listings Work**: You remembered correctly! For CRM clients, they have a landing page. But for **Listing clients**, they don't use standard landing pages. Instead, their properties show up on the main directory, and the **single property page** acts as the landing page. The inquiry form on that single property page automatically uses the client's API & ID to send leads straight into their pipeline.
   * **Regarding Ads**: We currently have a "Featured Listing" toggle. When checked, it pushes the property to the top of the search results (acting as an "Ad"). I will restrict this "Featured" checkbox so it is completely hidden/disabled for users on the Free plan.
2. **Featured Listings Restriction**: Confirmed. Only Silver and Gold will have access to it.
3. **Activity Logs Location**: I completely agree. I will add it as a new submenu item called "Activity Logs" (so it's easy to see everything globally), **AND** I will add a "Logs" tab inside each specific Client's page, so when you click a client, you can see only *their* history.
4. **Customizable Listing Caps**: We actually already built this! If you go to the **Settings** page in the backend and look for "Listing Plans", you can already change the max listings (caps) for each plan. I will simply update that settings panel to include the new "Free" plan, so you can change it from 1 to 2 or 3 whenever you want, directly from the backend.

